        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.083,
            0.885,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the North pole of a magnet is brought closer to the North pole of the compass needle, it moves away as shown in Fig. 4.9a. When the South pole of the magnet is brought closer to the North pole of the compass needle, it moves closer (Fig. 4.9b)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.379,
            0.213,
            0.626,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose we place a piece of wood between the compass needle and the magnet. Will this affect the deflection of the compass needle?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
